 <circle cx="505" cy="171" r="5" fill="#3e6d87"/><circle cx="484" cy="142" r="5" fill="#3e6d87"/><circle cx="462" cy="120" r="5" fill="#3e6d87"/>
-<text x="89" y="113" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,Verdana,sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#173039">Sun</text><text x="228" y="193" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,Verdana,sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#173039">light in</text><text x="465" y="48" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,Verdana,sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#173039">heat out</text><text x="431" y="212" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,Verdana,sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#173039">some held</text><text x="345" y="77" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,Verdana,sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#173039">CO₂ in air</text><text x="566" y="289" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,Verdana,sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#173039">fuel use</text></svg><figcaption>Light comes in. Earth releases heat. More CO₂ slows heat loss. Simplified mechanism; not to scale.</figcaption></figure><p class="model"><strong>Watch:</strong> Burn fossil fuel → add carbon dioxide → more heat stays → heat risks. Cut fuel use to cut emissions; plan shade to help with heat.</p><p><strong>Show me:</strong> Point to the cause card: burning fuel or a hotter day?</p><p data-mbm-guide>Model the full reasoning step, pre-teach four words and ask the show-me question.</p></section><section class="stage" id="we_do"><h2>We do · 7 min</h2><p>The burn fuel and impact cards are in place. Sort the missing gas and warming cards. Explain the link.</p><p class="model"><strong>Our turn:</strong> Burn fuel → add carbon dioxide → ____ → heat risks.</p><p>Talk, then sort.</p><form id="sort"><ul class="cards"><li data-answer="cause"><span>Burn fossil fuel</span><label>Group <select aria-label="Group for Burn fossil fuel"><option value="">Choose…</option><option>cause</option><option>middle link</option><option>impact</option><option>action</option></select></label><output aria-live="polite"></output></li><li data-answer="middle link"><span>More greenhouse gas</span><label>Group <select aria-label="Group for More greenhouse gas"><option value="">Choose…</option><option>cause</option><option>middle link</option><option>impact</option><option>action</option></select></label><output aria-live="polite"></output></li><li data-answer="impact"><span>Heat risk in some places</span><label>Group <select aria-label="Group for Heat risk in some places"><option value="">Choose…</option><option>cause</option><option>middle link</option><option>impact</option><option>action</option></select></label><output aria-live="polite"></output></li><li data-answer="action"><span>Cut fuel use</span><label>Group <select aria-label="Group for Cut fuel use"><option value="">Choose…</option><option>cause</option><option>middle link</option><option>impact</option><option>action</option></select></label><output aria-live="polite"></output></li></ul></form><div class="controls"><button type="button" id="check">Check the sort</button><button type="button" id="reset">Start again</button></div><p id="sort-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to sort.</p><div class="tiers"><div><h3>F · help</h3><p>Lay the first and last cards; point to each missing space before choosing a card.</p></div><div><h3>M · say why</h3><p>Explain two chain links.</p></div><div><h3>H · stretch</h3><p>Explain why a flood defence does not remove carbon dioxide already added by burning fuel.</p></div></div><section class="model" aria-label="Practical steps"><h3>Try it with kit</h3><p><strong>Guess first:</strong> Will ice on dark and light card melt alike?</p><p><strong>Kit:</strong> Two equal ice pieces · Two trays · Dark card · Light card · Staff clock</p><ol><li>Put equal ice pieces on cards in trays.</li><li>Place both trays in the same light.</li><li>Observe both at one set time.</li><li>Record what you see. Say why this is not a climate model.</li></ol><table><thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>dark card ice</th><th>light card ice</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Start</td><td>observation</td><td>observation</td></tr><tr><td>Later</td><td>observation</td><td>observation</td></tr></tbody></table><p data-mbm-guide>Check against the school risk assessment and CLEAPSS guidance. Dry spills; use no heat source. This surface observation is not proof of the greenhouse effect.</p></section><p data-mbm-guide>Show the part-done example, then allow paired talk before an answer. One-minute reset inside this stage.</p></section><section class="stage" id="we_do_2"><h2>We do 2 · 5 min</h2><p>Choose what follows burning more fossil fuel in our warming chain. Everyone answers together.</p><fieldset><legend><strong>Which action helps with an impact rather than cutting emissions?</strong></legend><div class="options"><label><input type="radio" name="other" value="right"> Flood defence</label><label><input type="radio" name="other" value="wrong"> Cut fuel use</label></div></fieldset><button type="button" id="other-check">Check the step</button><p id="other-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Choose a step.</p><p><strong>All of us:</strong> What belongs just after ‘burning more fossil fuel’ in this chain?</p><label>Show it: <select aria-label="Hinge response mode"><option>Point</option><option>Symbol card</option><option>Whiteboard</option><option>Finger vote</option><option>Thumbs</option></select></label><div class="options" role="group" aria-label="Choose one answer"><label><input type="radio" name="hinge" value="0"> More carbon dioxide in the air</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge" value="1"> Less daylight each day</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge" value="2"> The Earth stops spinning</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge" value="3"> Every place floods at once</label></div><p>Point. Tell a partner why.</p><p>Take one quiet minute to reset.</p><p data-mbm-guide>All pupils answer the four-option hinge; use the decision rule, not a score.</p></section><section class="stage" id="independent"><h2>Independent · 8 min</h2><p>Build a cause-to-impact chain. Compare an emissions cut with help for an impact. Give one reason for each.</p><p>Talk first. You can plan in any language.</p><p>Point, sign, speak, draw, type, write, use a scribe or show a staff-captured photo.</p><div class="tiers"><div><h3>F</h3><p>Order one cause and effect.</p><p><strong>Say first:</strong> First ___, then ___.</p></div><div><h3>M</h3><p>Explain two chain links.</p><p><strong>Say first:</strong> Burning ___ adds ___; this leads to ___ because ___.</p></div><div><h3>H</h3><p>Compare an emissions cut with an adaptation.</p><p><strong>Say first:</strong> Action A changes ___, while action B helps with ___; I would choose ___ because ___.</p></div></div><p class="stretch"><strong>Go deeper:</strong> Why might a council cut fuel use and plan flood defences? Name a limit of each.</p><p class="stretch"><strong>Two kinds of action:</strong> Choose a council goal, justify the first action and explain the problem still left.</p><p data-mbm-guide>One adult supports agreed pupils, the other holds the group; swap across the week. One-minute reset inside this stage.</p></section><section class="stage" id="review"><h2>Review · 4 min</h2><p>Hear feedback. Move one chain card and say why.</p><p>VF: hear one comment. NS(+): name a next step. //: edit one part. ?: ask for a read-back. Take one quiet minute.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Give a specific verbal comment (VF) and invite one self-edit (//) or read-back (?).</p></section><section class="stage" id="exit"><h2>Exit · 3 min</h2><p>Name a cause, an effect and an action. Which link does your action change?</p><p><strong>? Read it back:</strong> explain a cause and an effect of global warming, then compare two kinds of action.</p><p><strong>My feedback was…</strong> say what changed. <strong>Next I need to…</strong> name a fix.</p><p><strong>How I know:</strong> I can put cause before effect. I can say how gases add to warming. I can compare a cut in emissions with help for an impact.</p><p>The adult hears you and chooses our next example. Take one quiet minute.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Hear the answer and name how it changes the next example or support. One-minute reset and handoff.</p></section></main><footer>Offline lesson · no answers are saved</footer><script>(()=>{const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll('.cards li')],sort=document.getElementById('sort');const feedback=document.getElementById('sort-status');document.getElementById('check').addEventListener('click',()=>{cards.forEach(card=>{const value=card.querySelector('select').value;card.querySelector('output').textContent=value?(value===card.dataset.answer?'That fits.':'Look at the clue. Try again.'):'Choose a group.'});feedback.textContent='Check each card. Try again if you need.'});document.getElementById('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{sort.reset();cards.forEach(card=>card.querySelector('output').textContent='');document.querySelectorAll('input[type=radio]').forEach(el=>el.checked=false);document.getElementById('other-status').textContent='Choose a step.';feedback.textContent='Ready to sort.';sort.querySelector('select').focus()});document.getElementById('other-check').addEventListener('click',()=>{const x=document.querySelector('input[name=other]:checked');document.getElementById('other-status').textContent=x?(x.value==='right'?'Yes. Tell a partner why.':'Look at the model. Try again.'):'Choose a step.'});document.getElementById('calm').addEventListener('click',e=>{const on=document.body.classList.toggle('calm');e.currentTarget.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(on));e.currentTarget.textContent=on?'Calm view on':'Calm view off'});})();</script></body></html>
