ead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>run 1 (cm)</th><th>run 2 (cm)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rough</td><td>___</td><td>___</td></tr><tr><td>Smooth</td><td>___</td><td>___</td></tr></tbody></table><p data-mbm-guide>Check against the school risk assessment and CLEAPSS guidance. Keep the track low and clear; avoid raised drops and mains equipment. Do not invent or change results.</p></section><p data-mbm-guide>Show the part-done example, then allow paired talk before an answer. One-minute reset inside this stage.</p></section><section class="stage" id="we_do_2"><h2>We do 2 · 5 min</h2><p>Everyone chooses the fair plan for comparing two surfaces.</p><fieldset><legend><strong>What should you do if two repeat runs disagree?</strong></legend><div class="options"><label><input type="radio" name="other" value="right"> Keep results and check the method</label><label><input type="radio" name="other" value="wrong"> Alter one result to match</label></div></fieldset><button type="button" id="other-check">Check the step</button><p id="other-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Choose a step.</p><p><strong>All of us:</strong> Which plan is fairest for comparing rough and smooth surfaces?</p><label>Show it: <select aria-label="Hinge response mode"><option>Point</option><option>Symbol card</option><option>Whiteboard</option><option>Finger vote</option><option>Thumbs</option></select></label><div class="options" role="group" aria-label="Choose one answer"><label><input type="radio" name="hinge" value="0"> Change only the surface; use the same toy, start and launch</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge" value="1"> Change surface and starting line</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge" value="2"> Change surface and toy</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge" value="3"> Change the distance after each run</label></div><p>Point. Tell a partner why.</p><p>Take one quiet minute to reset.</p><p data-mbm-guide>All pupils answer the four-option hinge; use the decision rule, not a score.</p></section><section class="stage" id="independent"><h2>Independent · 8 min</h2><p>Test two runs per surface or observe. Record distance. Name what changed, stayed the same and could limit the test.</p><p>Talk first. You can plan in any language.</p><p>Point, sign, speak, draw, type, write, use a scribe or show a staff-captured photo.</p><div class="tiers"><div><h3>F</h3><p>Point to the factor that changes.</p><p><strong>Say first:</strong> I change the ___; I keep ___ the same.</p></div><div><h3>M</h3><p>Name two controls and record a result.</p><p><strong>Say first:</strong> I changed ___ and kept ___ the same. My result was ___.</p></div><div><h3>H</h3><p>Explain why repeat runs help and identify a method limit.</p><p><strong>Say first:</strong> My result suggests ___, but I would repeat ___ because ___.</p></div></div><p class="stretch"><strong>Go deeper:</strong> Two runs differ. Name a reason and fix a method step.</p><p class="stretch"><strong>Fair test repair:</strong> Two repeats differ. Name a safe conclusion, then improve the method for the next test.</p><p data-mbm-guide>One adult supports agreed pupils, the other holds the group; swap across the week. One-minute reset inside this stage.</p></section><section class="stage" id="review"><h2>Review · 4 min</h2><p>Check the controls and result with a partner. Fix one label before you conclude.</p><p>VF: hear one comment. NS(+): name a next step. //: edit one part. ?: ask for a read-back. Take one quiet minute.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Give a specific verbal comment (VF) and invite one self-edit (//) or read-back (?).</p></section><section class="stage" id="exit"><h2>Exit · 3 min</h2><p>Name the change, one control, one result and a next step.</p><p><strong>? Read it back:</strong> plan a fair investigation, record a result and explain a limit.</p><p><strong>My feedback was…</strong> say what changed. <strong>Next I need to…</strong> name a fix.</p><p><strong>How I know:</strong> I can name what I change and what I keep the same. I can record what happened in a small test. I can explain one way to make the test more dependable.</p><p>The adult hears you and chooses our next example. Take one quiet minute.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Hear the answer and name how it changes the next example or support. One-minute reset and handoff.</p></section></main><footer>Offline lesson · no answers are saved</footer><script>(()=>{const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll('.cards li')],sort=document.getElementById('sort');const feedback=document.getElementById('sort-status');document.getElementById('check').addEventListener('click',()=>{cards.forEach(card=>{const value=card.querySelector('select').value;card.querySelector('output').textContent=value?(value===card.dataset.answer?'That fits.':'Look at the clue. Try again.'):'Choose a group.'});feedback.textContent='Check each card. Try again if you need.'});document.getElementById('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{sort.reset();cards.forEach(card=>card.querySelector('output').textContent='');document.querySelectorAll('input[type=radio]').forEach(el=>el.checked=false);document.getElementById('other-status').textContent='Choose a step.';feedback.textContent='Ready to sort.';sort.querySelector('select').focus()});document.getElementById('other-check').addEventListener('click',()=>{const x=document.querySelector('input[name=other]:checked');document.getElementById('other-status').textContent=x?(x.value==='right'?'Yes. Tell a partner why.':'Look at the model. Try again.'):'Choose a step.'});document.getElementById('calm').addEventListener('click',e=>{const on=document.body.classList.toggle('calm');e.currentTarget.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(on));e.currentTarget.textContent=on?'Calm view on':'Calm view off'});})();</script></body></html>
